e":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The 'e' is omitted on purpose and for stylistc reasons... I promise.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13322-aneas","name":"Aneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13322_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:09:31-07:00","id":1108097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aneas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108081-beats-experiences-and-blood-sorcery-themes?p=1108093#post1108093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure there's a listed experience cost for themes, since the 'default' 2e system doesn't use them. If your are using the alternative system from the Blood Sorcery book, I personally have Themes costing 3 exp, and memorizing rituals costing only 1 exp since memorizing rituals aren't as vital or useful under those rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a simple formula for converting 1e exp costs to 2e experiences. What did Themes cost in 1e, 5xp times new dot? They'd cost 3 per dot in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-26-2017, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:11:12-07:00","id":1108098,"title":"","content":"Requiem's second edition does say you get a free Theme dot when you increase your Ritual Discipline ability, such as Cruac or Theban Sorcery or Nimosian Shadowmagic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:39:09-07:00","id":1108107,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> <br /> where is<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108081-beats-experiences-and-blood-sorcery-themes?p=1108098#post1108098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nimosian Shadowmagic.</div> </div> </div> </div>from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T16:47:09-07:00","id":1108187,"title":"","content":"I made it up. Technically from Achaea, I suppose. But it was a placeholder to represent the various blood sorceries that aren't as popular as Theban or Cruac but still offer access to Themes and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T18:59:19-07:00","id":1108214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108081-beats-experiences-and-blood-sorcery-themes?p=1108097#post1108097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a simple formula for converting 1e exp costs to 2e experiences. What did Themes cost in 1e, 5xp times new dot? They'd cost 3 per dot in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where can I find this formula? Is it Dev approved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T19:01:50-07:00","id":1108217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108081-beats-experiences-and-blood-sorcery-themes?p=1108187#post1108187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made it up. Technically from Achaea, I suppose. But it was a placeholder to represent the various blood sorceries that aren't as popular as Theban or Cruac but still offer access to Themes and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. It sounded cool. I was wondering how I could have missed something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T19:17:23-07:00","id":1108224,"title":"","content":"&quot;Theme dots may be bought independently of the Ritual<br /> Discipline for (new rating x 5) Experience&quot;<br /> <br /> Themes used to cost as much as Attributes so it would be easy enough to stick with that. I think the formula the Devs had offered was 3 dots times cost multiplier divided by 5, or 3 in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T21:32:11-07:00","id":1108260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108081-beats-experiences-and-blood-sorcery-themes?p=1108214#post1108214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I find this formula? Is it Dev approved?</div> </div> </div> </div>I reverse-engineered it based on the way Beats and Experiences work in 2e as compared to how Experience Points work in 1e, and verified it with Attributes, Skills, Merits, and In-Clan and Out-Of-Clan Disciplines. David Hill indirectly confirmed it when I observed that Attributes didn't seem to follow the formula for some reason (see below), and he explained what I was missing and why they do.<br /> <br /> Basically, costs in 1e scale exponentially (&quot;X times new dot&quot;), whereas costs in 2e are all &quot;flat&quot; (X per dot). So you have to find the mean cost per dot in 1e by summing the experience cost for each dot and dividing by the number of dots. Conveniently, for anything with a zero-to-five scale, the result will be the same as the cost of the third dot. So taking the trait in question, Themes, Themes can be rated from 0 to 5. The first dot costs 5xp, the second costs 10xp, the third costs 15xp, the fourth costs 20xp, and the fifth costs 25xp. 5+10+15+20+25=75 and 75/5=15. So the mean cost per dot is 15, same as the cost of the third dot.<br /> <br /> Then, since each 2e experience is 5 Beats, and Beats are awarded at approximately the same rate as 1e xp, we have to divide our mean cost by 5 to find its equivalent in 2e experiences. 15/5=3, so Theme dots in 2e cost 3 experiences, same as an in-Clan Discipline, which is also 5 times new dot xp in 1e and 3 experiences in 2e.<br /> <br /> You can confirm that this works with the other traits as well, just remember to round to the nearest whole number when you divide the mean cost by 5. It doesn't work with Blood Potency, but the devs have confirmed that they lowered the cost of Power Stat dots in 2e relative to their cost in 1e because they want people to actually consider buying them and they were prohibitively expensive in 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108081-beats-experiences-and-blood-sorcery-themes?p=1108224#post1108224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Theme dots may be bought independently of the Ritual<br /> Discipline for (new rating x 5) Experience&quot;<br /> <br /> Themes used to cost as much as Attributes so it would be easy enough to stick with that. I think the formula the Devs had offered was 3 dots times cost multiplier divided by 5, or 3 in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Close, but it's actually mean cost per dot divided by 5. It just happens to work out that the third dot of anything that goes from 0 to 5 dots is conveniently the same as the mean cost per dot. But It doesn't work out that way with Attributes, because you never actually have to pay for the first dot, making the mean cost per dot 17.5 instead of 15. (10+15+20+25=70 and 70/4=17.5). When you divide the mean cost per dot for Attributes by 5 you get 3.5, and rounding to the nearest whole number gives you 4 experiences per dot in 2e, as opposed to the 3 experiences per dot we get for Theme dots and In-Clan Disciplines above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-27-2017, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}